6. Closure & Function Manipulation
Function	Signature	Description
newcclosure	(f: function) → function	Wraps Lua function in C closure. iscclosure returns true. Preferred for anti-tamper.
newlclosure	(f: function) → function	Wraps in a Lua closure.
wrapclosure	(f: function) → function	Generic wrap — picks appropriate closure type.
clonefunction	(f: function) → function	Structurally identical clone with distinct identity.
hookfunction	(target: function, hook: function) → function	Redirects all calls to target through hook. Returns original. Aliases: hookfunc, replacefunction, replaceclosure
hookmetamethod	(object: any, method: string, hook: function) → function	Hooks a metamethod (__index, __namecall, etc.).
iscclosure	(f) → boolean	true if f is a C function.
islclosure	(f) → boolean	true if f is a Lua function.
isnewcclosure	(f) → boolean	true if f came from newcclosure.
isexecutorclosure	(f) → boolean	true if f is created/wrapped by Velocity. Aliases: checkclosure, isourclosure, iscustomcclosure, istempleclosure, is_synapse_function, issentinelclosure, is_sirhurt_closure, is_protosmasher_closure
comparefunctions	(a: function, b: function) → boolean	true if both dispatch to same target (unwraps clones).
getfunctionhash	(f: function) → string	Stable hash of function's bytecode.
isfunctionhooked	(f: function) → boolean	true if f has an active hookfunction installed.
restorefunction	(f: function)	Removes any hook installed on f. Aliases: restorefunc
getcallbackvalue	(object: any, memberName: string) → function?	Read current Lua callback on a callback member. Aliases: getcallbackmember
getcallstack	() → {table}	Full callstack — each entry has source, func, currentline, name, what.
