10. Signals & Events
Function	Signature	Description
firesignal	(signal: RBXScriptSignal, ...args)	Invoke every Connect/Once handler and resume every Wait. Deep-marshals table args, preserves Instance identity.
defersignal	(signal: RBXScriptSignal, ...args)	Same as firesignal but dispatches via task.defer.
replicatesignal	(signal: RBXScriptSignal, ...args)	Fire a signal AND replicate it to the server (for allowlisted events).
cansignalreplicate	(signal: RBXScriptSignal) → boolean	Whether replicatesignal is allowed on this event.
getconnections	(signal: RBXScriptSignal) → {Connection}	All connections on the signal. Each exposes: Function, Thread, Enabled, ForeignState, plus :Fire, :Defer, :Disconnect, :Disable, :Enable.
fireclickdetector	(clickDetector: ClickDetector, distance: number?)	Simulate a click at given distance.
fireproximityprompt	(prompt: ProximityPrompt)	Trigger a proximity prompt as if local player held it.
getsignalarguments	(signal: RBXScriptSignal) → {string}	Type names of each argument the signal fires with.
getsignalargumentsinfo	(signal: RBXScriptSignal) → {{Name:string, Type:string}}	Full argument info — name and type per parameter.
getsignalwhitelist	() → {{Event:string, Parent:string}}	Events on which replicatesignal is permitted.
Userland Signal API (Signal.new):

Method	Signature	Description
Signal.new	() → Signal	Creates a fresh userland signal object.
sig:Connect	(handler: function) → Connection	Register a handler. Returns a Connection with :Disconnect().
sig:Once	(handler: function) → Connection	Register a one-shot handler.
sig:Wait	() → ...args	Yield until next Fire; returns its args.
sig:Fire	(...args)	Dispatch to every connected handler (via task.spawn) and resume every waiting thread.
conn:Disconnect	()	Release callback ref and unlink from parent signal.
