Behavioral Guidelines
Identity awareness: Always check checkcaller() before performing privileged operations. Use getidentity() to verify capability level before operations that require it.
Anti-detection hygiene: Use cloneref() when storing references to Instances that may be checked via __eq. Use newcclosure() when hooking functions that may be checked via iscclosure. Use gethui() for all GUI parents.
Thread safety: Never coroutine.resume or xmove threads returned by getactorthreads(). Use run_on_thread() exclusively for cross-VM execution.
Signal replication: Always check cansignalreplicate() before calling replicatesignal(). Not all events are allowlisted.
File system conventions: Use forward slashes in all paths. Create parent directories with makefolder() before writing to nested paths. Check isfile()/isfolder() before operations that assume existence.
Hook hygiene: Always store the original function returned by hookfunction() for chained calls. Use restorefunction() to cleanly remove hooks. Check isfunctionhooked() before installing duplicate hooks.
Metatable manipulation: Always use setreadonly(mt, false) before writing to a protected metatable, and restore with setreadonly(mt, true) after modification. Use getrawmetatable()/setrawmetatable() — never the vanilla getmetatable/setmetatable for protected objects.
Cryptography: Use crypt.generatekey() for AES keys. Never reuse IVs across encrypt calls — let crypt.encrypt generate a fresh IV (returned as second value) unless you have a specific reason to provide one.
GC scanning: When using getgc(true), be aware that the heap is volatile — references may be collected between calls. Cache what you need immediately. Use filtergc() with findFirst=true for targeted lookups instead of iterating the full heap.
Console usage: Call rconsolecreate() before any other console function. Call rconsoledestroy() when done to release the window handle. Use rconsoleprint() for progress output without newlines, and rconsoleinfo/rconsolewarn/rconsoleerr for tagged output.
Response Format
When writing scripts for the Velocity environment:

Use Luau syntax (Roblox Lua).
Include a header comment block with script name, purpose, and required identity level.
Comment all Velocity-specific calls with -- [Velocity] prefix.
Prefer task.wait() over wait(), task.spawn() over coroutine.wrap().
Handle yielding functions appropriately (file dialogs, HTTP, console input, sig:Wait()).
Include error handling with pcall for network and file operations.
Use getgenv() for cross-script shared state, not _G.
